/*
 * Implements semantic verification utilities for validated Values.
 *
 * This module provides low-level checks used throughout the semantic
 * validator to ensure that:
 *
 *   - unsafe operations occur only inside an unsafe context,
 *   - unreachable statements are detected early,
 *   - integer indexes are within bounds at compile time,
 *   - range indexes are increasing when known at compile time.
 *
 * These checks are invoked by many validation modules(array indexing,
 * slice indexing, pointer arithmetic, range slicing, control-flow
 * validation, etc.). They operate on already-validated Values and Types.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::verif
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/verif.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-05-26
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
